│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ personal_voice_forum_register                                                             │
│ patch_description        │ Almost every flagged output reads like a tidy explainer. It opens with a topic sentence,  │
│                          │ then each sentence adds one fact in neutral, encyclopedic third person, with no speaker   │
│                          │ present. The target examples that passed as human have a different set of traits:         │
│                          │ - They are first person and have a speaker with a stance ("I guess", "I mean", "I would   │
│                          │ not steer people away").                                                                  │
│                          │ - They hedge and qualify.                                                                 │
│                          │ - They ask rhetorical questions.                                                          │
│                          │ - They carry asides in parentheses.                                                       │
│                          │ - They use contractions and loosely joined clauses ("and not only did they..., but").     │
│                          │ - They react to the situation instead of laying out a lecture.                            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This edit rewrites the prompt toward a forum-reply register: a person talking from their  │
│                          │ own experience or opinion, mixing explanation with reaction and an uneven order. It adds  │
│                          │ explicit bans on explainer scaffolding such as "The short answer is", definitions opening │
│                          │ the text, and "That is why". It keeps the instructions to reason briefly, invent no facts │
│                          │ and respect length, so task scores and the empty-output rate stay healthy. Invented       │
│                          │ personal facts are forbidden, but opinion and hedging are allowed.                        │
